title: guarding *new* tests on an optional dependency disables nothing
origin: adversarial audit 2026-08-07, and it is a regression this project
origin2: shipped the same day: the v0.1.9 rule that stops repair evidence from
origin3: excusing a collection control did not ask whether the control was
origin4: guarded. So a PR that adds a backend, adds its tests, and gates them
origin5: on `find_spec` blocked at high — with `NO_PROD_CHANGE_IN_DIFF` printed
origin6: over a diff that changes three production files. Net tests disabled: 0.
